# =============================================================================
# Decoy-samba — the SMB endpoint OpenCanary watches
#
# Samba with full_audit + rsyslog writing the audit feed onto the shared
# decoy_logs volume; OpenCanary (decoy-opencanary) tails that file and alerts.
# The share is fake, the host is isolated (decoy-net, internal), and nothing
# here is a real credential. The rootfs is read-only at runtime (compose) —
# the share itself only accepts writes that fail, which the audit still logs.
# =============================================================================

FROM debian:bookworm-slim

ARG VIGIL_VERSION=
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.version="${VIGIL_VERSION}"
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.title="vigil-decoy-samba"

RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
      samba \
      samba-vfs-modules \
      rsyslog \
      smbclient \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

COPY infra/docker/decoy/smb.conf /etc/samba/smb.conf
COPY infra/docker/decoy/rsyslog-samba.conf /etc/rsyslog.d/30-samba-audit.conf
COPY infra/docker/decoy/samba-entrypoint.sh /usr/local/bin/decoy-samba-entrypoint
RUN chmod +x /usr/local/bin/decoy-samba-entrypoint \
    && mkdir -p /srv/decoy-share

EXPOSE 445

HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=5s --start-period=20s --retries=3 \
  CMD smbclient -L localhost -N >/dev/null 2>&1

ENTRYPOINT ["/usr/local/bin/decoy-samba-entrypoint"]
